\pard\keep\keepn\sb480\sl276\slmult1\cf1\b\f2\fs28 1. What is this assignment about?\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\cf0\b0\f0\fs21 This is not a memorization assignment. Your goal is to explore AI yourself, understand the basic concepts, and explain them in simple words. You are expected to search, watch short videos if needed, use AI tools for clarification, and compare information from multiple sources.\par
Important: Do not simply copy an AI-generated answer. Use AI as a learning assistant, then rewrite the ideas in your own words and add your own examples.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\sb480\sl276\slmult1\cf1\b\f2\fs28 2. Learning Goals\par

\pard{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf7\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li360\sa200\sl276\slmult1\tx360\cf0\b0\f0\fs21 Understand what Artificial Intelligence means at a high level.\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Clearly distinguish AI, Machine Learning, Deep Learning, and Generative AI.\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Identify real-world AI use cases across different industries.\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Understand the major career paths available in AI and related technology roles.\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Explain the concepts in your own words instead of relying on textbook definitions.\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Apply the concepts to a practical real-world example.\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Identify common misunderstandings or errors and improve your explanation.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\sb480\sl276\slmult1\cf1\b\f2\fs28 3. Your Mission\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\cf0\b0\f0\fs21 Imagine that a friend who knows nothing about AI asks you: \ldblquote What exactly is AI, what is the difference between AI, ML, DL and GenAI, where is AI used, and what can I become if I learn AI?\rdblquote\par
Your job is to create a beginner-friendly answer that your friend can understand in 10 minutes.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\sb480\sl276\slmult1\cf1\b\f2\fs28 4. Step 1 \f1\endash\f2  Explore: What is AI?\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\cf0\b0\f0\fs21 Do your own research and answer the following questions:\par
1. What is Artificial Intelligence in your own words?\par
A.Artificial intelligence  is a technology that enables machines /computers to perform tasks that normally require human intelligence\par
2. What makes a system 'intelligent'?\par
A intelligent system is a system that can learn from data , understand information, solve promblems and make decisions\par
3. Give at least 5 examples of AI that you may interact with in daily life.\par
A.face recognition,voice recognition, recommendation system, google maps, error detection,\par
4. Choose one AI example and explain what the system is doing.\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1 A. Youtube recommendation-When we watch a video on YouTube, search for videos, like them, or skip them, YouTube analyzes our activity to understand our interests. Based on this, it recommends videos that match our interests.\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1 5. Is every software application an AI application? Explain why or why not.\par
No. Not every software application is an AI application. Some software only follows fixed instructions and does not learn or make decisions. AI applications can learn from data and perform tasks that need human-like intelligence.\par
6. What are 2 things AI can do well and 2 things AI may struggle with?\par
A. 1.Analyze large amounts of data quickly.\par
    2. understand speech\par
AI MAY STRUGGLE WITH :\par
   1.Humans emotions does't  understand\par
    2.Giving correct answers all the time, especially when the data is incomplete or wrong.\par
\par
Research rule: Use at least 3 learning sources. These can be articles, videos, official documentation, or educational websites.\par
Tip: Try searching for simple explanations first. If two sources disagree, investigate why.\par

