Now answer these questions:\par
1. Is ML a part of AI? Explain with a simple example.\par
 A.Yes. ML is \ldblquote a method of AI training\rdblquote  and is the \ldblquote engine\rdblquote  which underlies most of modern AI. Think of AI as the overarching concept, with ML nested inside of it. A simple example would be the spam filter in your email. Instead of a human writing a permanent rule of what looks like spam, ML learns regularities from data sets to find junk mail automatically. \par
2. Is Deep Learning a type of Machine Learning? Explain.\par
a. Yes. Deep Learning is a type of Machine Learning that uses neural networks with multiple layers to learn complex patterns from data.\par
3. Is Generative AI the same thing as AI? Why?\par
No. AI is the broad, \ldblquote overarching concept\rdblquote  of making machines act or think like humans. Generative AI is essentially the exact opposite of broad, and it is in fact the most \ldblquote deepest layer of AI.\rdblquote  While a standard AI might use basic logic to solve a problem, GenAI is programmed to parse through natural language or images to generate original content (such as ChatGPT)\par
4. Can an AI system exist without Machine Learning? Research and explain one example\par
.A.Yes. An AI system can exist without Machine Learning. Some AI systems use predefined rules and logic instead of learning from data. Example: chess game\par
