\pard\keep\keepn\sb480\sl276\slmult1\cf1\b\f2\fs28 10. Step 7 \f1\endash\f2  Common Errors: Find and Fix Them\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\cf0\b0\f0\fs21 For each statement below, decide whether it is correct, partially correct, or incorrect. Then explain why.\par
1. \ldblquote AI and Machine Learning are exactly the same thing.\rdblquote\par
Your verdict + correction: NO ,Artificial intelligence is technology that enables computers to perform tasks that normally require human intelligence and Ml is a subset of ai ,that enables computers to learn from data improve their performance without being explicity programmed for every task\par
2. \ldblquote Deep Learning is unrelated to Machine Learning.\rdblquote\par
Your verdict + correction: NO,ML and DL both learn from data. DL is a type of ML that uses multiple layers of neural networks to learn complex patterns, especially from large amounts of data.\par
3."ChatGPT is just a search engine"\par
Your verdict + correction:No. ChatGPT is not just a search engine. It is a Generative AI system that can understand questions and generate answers, explanations, summaries, and other content.\par
4. \ldblquote Generative AI always gives correct answers.\rdblquote\par
Your verdict + correction: NO,because Generative AI does not always give correct answers. It can sometimes provide incorrect or misleading information.\par
5. \ldblquote If a company uses AI, it does not need humans anymore.\rdblquote\par
Your verdict + correction: NO,. AI can help humans perform tasks faster and more efficiently, but humans are still needed for decision-making, creativity, communication, problem-solving, and managing AI systems.\par
6. \ldblquote More data automatically means a better AI system.\rdblquote\par
Your verdict + correction: No. More data does not always make an AI system better. The data should be accurate, relavent and high-quality\par

